[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1648385143","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1648385143","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1648385143,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85iQFx3","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-24T18:19:46Z","updated_at":"2023-07-24T18:19:46Z","body":"This was approved for Fedora: see https://gitlab.com/fedora/legal/fedora-license-data/-/issues/223","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1648385143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1649911473","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1649911473","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1649911473,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85iV6ax","user":{"login":"mcb30","id":692245,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MjI0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/692245?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30","html_url":"https://github.com/mcb30","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mcb30/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T14:04:48Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T14:04:48Z","body":"For the record: there are no files in iPXE licensed solely under the UBDL.  All affected files are dual-licensed under GPLv2+ or UBDL.  The fact that the UBDL text itself refers to the GPL is orthogonal to this: the files may be treated as licensed under either the GPLv2+ or under [some other license].\r\n\r\nFor simplicity, I would suggest that Fedora or other distributors choose the GPLv2+ option and be done with it.\r\n\r\nIn case it's relevant: the motivation for creating the UBDL is that some OEMs refuse to ship BIOS images that will incur the GPL obligations of providing source code.  They have no interest in creating a closed-source version of iPXE: they just won't subject themselves to the process obligations of dealing with source code requests from end users.  Hence the structure of the UBDL to allow obligation-free redistribution of the binary when the source code to that binary is already available to the world at large.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1649911473/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1652628326","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1652628326","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1652628326,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85igRtm","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-26T22:34:32Z","updated_at":"2023-07-26T22:34:32Z","body":"@mcb30 While Fedora could explicitly pick GPLv2+ (~ SPDX `GPL-2.0-or-later` :) , the longstanding tradition in Fedora is to pass through upstream license choices unless one of the choices is considered 'bad' or not allowed (and even then, generally the disallowed license is ignored in the metadata but is not removed from source code license notices). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1652628326/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659059733","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1659059733","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1659059733,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85i4z4V","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-31T20:08:39Z","updated_at":"2023-07-31T20:09:49Z","body":"to be clear, this is not a standalone license, so the SPDX expression would be: `GPL-2.0-or-later WITH <iPXE-UBDL-exception>`\r\n\r\nas to the SPDX inclusion principles for exceptions:\r\n\r\n- The exception is not a stand-alone license. - YES\r\nThe exception either:\r\n- grants an exception to a license condition; and/or - YES\r\n- grants an addition permission beyond those granted in a license.\r\n- The exception does not impose additional restrictions or limitations beyond those granted in the underlying license. - IT DOES NOT\r\n- The exception has actual, substantial use such that it is likely to be encountered. - USED IN A MAJOR DISTRO (FEDORA), SO YES\r\n\r\nmeant to add: so I would be in favor of adding it","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659059733/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659131616","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1659131616","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1659131616,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85i5Fbg","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-31T20:40:54Z","updated_at":"2023-07-31T20:40:54Z","body":"I'm a bit conflicted on naming - we usually try to honor whatever is used \"in the wild\" if applicable, but I kind of have issue with UBDL due to the L standing for license...","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1659131616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1673454176","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1673454176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1673454176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85jvuJg","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-10T15:29:45Z","updated_at":"2023-08-10T15:29:45Z","body":"I'm +1 to add, but I would add this as a license rather than as an exception. My main reasons for this are:\r\n\r\n- As mentioned, the upstream project is treating it as a standalone license (and has titled it as such)\r\n- In similar cases (such as LGPL-3.0), I think we've _generally_ leaned towards taking the upstream's perspective on this\r\n- Also, the first condition (lines 50-54) I think _arguably_ imposes an additional condition that goes beyond [the underlying GPL-2.0 license's requirement in Section 2(c)](https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/gpl-2.0.en.html).\r\n  - Reasoning: GPL-2.0 section 2(c) only requires displaying announcements for interactive programs that normally print copyright notices, etc.; but the iPXE version appears to require displaying the announcement \"when starting running\" the Program in all circumstances.\r\n\r\nBetween all of the above points, I think I would treat this as a license for the License List rather than a license exception. That said, I do think this is an edge case and I could be convinced otherwise  :)\r\n\r\nWhether it is to be treated as its own license or as an exception, I'm +1 to add it and I think it meets either set of requirements.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1673454176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1674081253","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1674081253","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1674081253,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85jyHPl","user":{"login":"Pizza-Ria","id":46799628,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2Nzk5NjI4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46799628?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria","html_url":"https://github.com/Pizza-Ria","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Pizza-Ria/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-11T00:22:09Z","updated_at":"2023-08-11T00:22:09Z","body":"+1 to Exception.  For the factor:  The exception does not impose additional restrictions or limitations - I do agree with @swinslow that \"the Program must display an announcement which includes the details of your existing publication of the Program made in accordance with the terms of the GNU General Public License.\" appears to be an additional CONDITION but I don't interpret that to be a restriction/limitation.  ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1674081253/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1696723369","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1696723369","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1696723369,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85lIfGp","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-29T03:46:37Z","updated_at":"2023-08-29T03:46:37Z","body":"ok, so @swinslow made me re-review this, but I'm still at +1 as an Exception. I think @Pizza-Ria 's additional point is a good one. I think I also keep going back to - it's not a standalone license in anyway.\r\n\r\nas to the LGPL-3.0 example, that is the only time we have treated what is technically really an exception as a license which was more of a nod to not upsetting what people were used to in that particular case (and which has been re-hashed in multiple ways a few time, so this is not an invitation for another re-hashing ;)\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1696723369/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1699394631","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043#issuecomment-1699394631","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2043","id":1699394631,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85lSrRH","user":{"login":"mcb30","id":692245,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY5MjI0NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/692245?v=4","gravatar_id"